WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.310
Run one small change with open code in spec with code. This

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.850
walkthrough prepares the task. It does not submit a provider

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:08.130
run.

00:00:08.883 --> 00:00:12.203
Install and authenticate open code on the machine running the

00:00:12.203 --> 00:00:16.843
project. Then enable it in Settings, Providers. Refresh

00:00:16.843 --> 00:00:20.623
provider status after changing a login. Select a model your

00:00:20.623 --> 00:00:22.563
configured provider actually offers.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:26.810
Open an example repository as a project. The main

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:30.890
conversation is the project coordinator. Check which machine

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:31.750
is doing the work.

00:00:32.517 --> 00:00:36.257
Select Open Code, an available model, and the approval mode

00:00:36.257 --> 00:00:39.877
you intend to use. This tutorial does not require full

00:00:39.877 --> 00:00:40.277
access.

00:00:41.183 --> 00:00:45.543
Give it one bounded task. Add a named greeting, keep the no

00:00:45.543 --> 00:00:49.783
argument greeting working, and add tests for both. Ask it to

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:51.663
describe the change before editing.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:56.810
Read the proposed change, then ask it to implement. Review

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:59.930
any command approval rather than accepting it automatically.

00:01:00.983 --> 00:01:05.123
Inspect the changed files and the actual test output. If a

00:01:05.123 --> 00:01:09.323
check failed or was not run, keep that in the result. A

00:01:09.323 --> 00:01:11.803
confident reply is not test evidence.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:16.810
Finish with the change, its diff and actual test evidence.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:20.730
Use specweave increments when you need a durable plan and

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.770
task record. They are optional for this first task.
